  "boundaries": [
    "Two controls fail against unchanged original production. Nine final metadata and three store controls pass using finite offline fixtures; full CL suite passes 405 tests with one existing ignore.",
    "B3-73 covers authenticated metadata whose former durable or volatile owners have ended. Required anchors, current/latest targets, checkpoint and pending/recovery dependencies keep exact cached decreasing-slot ancestry.",
    "The writer returns same-height replaced-root candidates only after durable publication. Same beacon root at other heights remains supported; fresh borrowed membership handles aliases and reownership.",
    "Snapshot ownership checks, demotion and optional FIFO removal share one lock without I/O, await or nested ConsensusStore calls. This does not provide a generic observer/reconstruction protocol for arbitrary future external store mutations.",
    "Release work uses an ephemeral descending-slot heap and existing adjacency. No new per-anchor reverse index, permanent child counters or trusted-history cap. Ordinary unchanged and advancing-head controls add no retained-history scan.",
    "A real unresolved release batch may scan O(N) retained anchors once. Affected graph work, temporary allocation and existing FIFO costs remain; no throughput, total memory or constant-time guarantee is claimed.",
    "Whole response ownership spans nested processing and early returns. Draft missing-owner and changed-parent promotion defects were corrected before final validation. One old fixture now explicitly persists its retained head after real target switching, preserving every original assertion.",
    "Borrowed startup/target/seed/materialization summaries remove unnecessary history or committee clones in the touched readers. No new dependency, storage encoding, durability barrier or quota was introduced.",
    "An obsolete fork selected after optional eviction may require refetch. Eligible gossip cache overload, priority queues, shared query resources, dashboard, verified repair and integrated acceptance remain open.",
    "No new benchmark campaign, live sync, production data, remote-host work or release-readiness claim."
  ]
